  "prefLabel": "Sphc 102.06 Hearing aid",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Sphc 102.06 \"Hearing aid\" means “hearing aid” as defined in RSA 326-F:1, IV, namely, “any wearable instrument or device designed for or offered for the purpose of or represented as aiding or compensating for impaired human hearing and any parts or attachments, including ear molds, but excluding batteries and cords or accessories thereto, or equipment, devices, and attachments used in conjunction with services provided by a public utility company.”\n\nSource. #14193, eff 2-12-25",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/sphc100.html"
}
